course: dictionary
lesson: 13353
title: What is a handbook?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A handbook is a small book that gives useful facts and instructions about one subject, or rules about a place. «The school handbook tells us when lunch starts and what time we go home.» The clues are school, times and home, so a handbook must be a book full of useful information.
explain: Handbook is made of two words: hand and book. A handbook is a book small enough to keep close at hand, so you can grab it and look things up quickly. «Ella used her bird handbook to find out what the bird was called.» Ella needed facts about birds, so she looked in a book that gives facts.
explain: Many groups have handbooks. «Our Guide handbook shows us how to light a campfire safely.» Clubs, Scouts, Guides and workers each have a handbook with the rules and facts they need. When you meet a new word, ask: what kind of book would have that information?
fact: A handbook is a small book that gives useful facts and instructions.
fact: «Handbook» can also mean a book of rules for a place, such as a school or a club.
fact: Schools, clubs, Scouts, Guides and workers may all have a handbook.
fact: A field handbook helps you identify birds or plants.
fact: To find something in a handbook, look for the rules or facts you need.
exercise: «The new school handbook tells us the rules and the times for lunch.» What is a handbook? | A very large table for eating lunch | *A small book of useful facts, instructions or rules | A kind of school bell | A bag for carrying books
exercise: «Ella used her bird handbook to find out the name of the bird.» What was the handbook used for? | To play a game outside | To cook a dinner | To write a letter to a friend | *To find facts about birds
exercise: Mum says, «Check the club handbook for the rules.» Find and copy the word that names the book. | club | *handbook | rules | Mum
test: «Our Guide handbook shows us how to light a campfire safely.» What does the handbook show? | *How to light a campfire safely | The time of the school bus | The name of the Guide leader's dog | A recipe for a cake
test: Where would you look to find the rules of a club? | In a cookery book about cakes | *In the club handbook | In the sky | On the moon
exam: «The field handbook helped the scientists name the plant they found.» What does a field handbook help you do? | Sing a song | *Identify birds or plants | Bake bread | Swim faster
